__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
*.log
pending_updates.json
docker-compose.dev.yml

# Local notes — private, never pushed
IDEAS.md

# Local maintainer stats — pull counts and the script that fetches them.
# Deliberately never pushed: the individual figures are public on Docker
# Hub, but an hourly history builds a growth curve that exists nowhere
# else, and this repo is public.
.stats/

# Internal maintainer tooling — not part of what Docksentry ships.
# Anything named here also stays out of the CHANGELOG, because the
# what's-new notice builds its headlines from it and users have no use
# for our workflow.
scripts/issue_inbox.py

# Agent worktrees and session state. Tooling, not the project — and
# the worktrees are embedded git repositories, which git would either
# swallow as a broken submodule or copy wholesale.
.claude/

# Backups of the dev compose file — it holds real credentials, and a
# name the ignore list did not cover once got one committed.
docker-compose.dev.yml.*
*.bak-*

# Local backup bundles. They carry every channel credential the
# instance has, and three of them were committed to a public repo
# before this line existed (18.10.2026 — checked: those three held no
# settings, so nothing leaked, but the mechanism was live).
backups/

# Audit results stay on this machine. They describe, in order, what is
# not fixed yet — which for a self-hosted tool is a map of every running
# instance out there. Standing rule, 19.10.2026.
audit-reports/
